# core.autocrlf is true on this machine. Git's binary heuristic has so far
# classified these correctly, but a PDF that happens to contain no NUL byte in
# its first 8000 bytes would be treated as text, get its CRLFs rewritten, and
# arrive corrupted in a fresh clone -- while every local check still passes.
# Declare it instead of relying on the guess.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
